    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Studio Moniker was an Amsterdam interactive design studio founded in 2012 by Luna Maurer, Roel Wouters, and Jonathan Puckey (Puckey left 2016); closed 2023 when Luna and Roel ended the studio and moved to independent practices. Peak team around 6 people (co-founders plus Tjerk Woudsma, Jolana Sykorova, Thomas Boland, Grischa Erbe). Work spanned participatory web experiences, physical installations, print, video, and performance; known for Conditional Design methodology (rule-based systems that generate unpredictable outcomes). Clients included Google, Apple, Mozilla Foundation, Walker Art Center, Stedelijk Museum, Het Nieuwe Instituut. Won British Music Video Award, two Dutch Design Awards, Amsterdamprijs voor de Kunst. Founders continue independently under designingfriction.com (joint) and personal sites. Autonomy: N/A (studio entity, not a person). Capabilities sourced: studiomoniker.com/about + itsnicethat.com feature 2020.",
